        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(msteams): cap team-group-id cache with pruneMapToMaxSize",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`teamGroupIdCache` in `resolveTeamGroupId` had TTL-based expiry (10 min) but no size cap. A large Teams workspace with many distinct team IDs could accumulate entries faster than the TTL window.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded a 500-entry cap via `pruneMapToMaxSize` — the shared SDK helper already used by 10 other files across 5 extensions. Single-line addition after each cache write.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMemory bounded at ~500 entries regardless of workspace size. No behavioral change.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Same helper, same pattern — 10 existing call sites across the codebase\n\n`pruneMapToMaxSize` is the established SDK helper for capping module-level Maps. Every channel extension that caches external identifiers uses it — except `graph-thread.ts`:\n\n```\nDiscord:    extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-channel-info.ts:53\nNextcloud:  extensions/nextcloud-talk/src/room-info.ts:35\nSlack:      extensions/slack/src/channel-type.ts:35          (same PR #101562)\nSlack:      extensions/slack/src/monitor/thread-resolution.ts:99\nSlack:      extensions/slack/src/monitor/thread.ts:43\nGateway:    src/infra/dedupe.ts:50\nSDK:        src/plugin-sdk/webhook-memory-guards.ts:135,142,209\nSDK:        src/plugin-sdk/webhook-request-guards.ts:135\n```\n\n### Our change — one line, same pattern\n\n```diff\nextensions/msteams/src/graph-thread.ts:\n+  pruneMapToMaxSize(teamGroupIdCache, TEAM_GROUP_ID_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES);\n```\n\nNo new abstraction, no new import path, no behavior change for normal operation.\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex",
